{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790995917,"nonce":"R3HBY5ywjMRMOlD6niHv0pDiR4M=","title":"FixedThreadPool job never runs or never releases: main blocks forever in Lock.wait","message":"Reported by the ChimpMonk physics session at ash 1210987, macOS arm64, AOT binary.\n\nChimpMonk split its narrowphase across 4 workers with `sys.thread.FixedThreadPool`: one `pool.run` per worker, then a `Lock` join (`done.wait()` once per job), four dispatches per `World.step`. Roughly 1 run in 13 hung: the main thread blocked forever in `done.wait()` (lock_wait / semaphore_wait) while every ash-vm worker was idle. So a job either never ran or ran without its `release()` reaching the waiter. The same symptom appeared once in ChimpMonk's IslandParallelChecks (about 1 in 57 runs), which dispatches only once per substep.\n\nResults matched the serial run whenever it completed.\n\n**Reproducer:** no standalone one yet. The AOT binary that hit it:\n`/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-amaterasu-Vibranium-chimpmonk/5b7b99c6-d14a-4e10-8ac0-072885ae4da9/scratchpad/bin/pg`, run as `ASH_WORKERS=4 bin/pg stacks3d 4` in a loop under a timeout. It lives in a session scratchpad and is temporary. ChimpMonk has reverted the change; its notes are in ChimpMonk's issue git-bug 42d4f5bbb1caed50a9c5e283b9173a63e6017640c685b233c0843c3532e1d72a.\n\nThe machine was under heavy load (another session's rustc builds, load 30-190) when this was seen, which widens any lost-wakeup window.","files":null}]}